{"1-4":{"people":[{"id":"jehoshaphat-h3092i","name":"Jehoshaphat","kind":"person","brief":"King of Judah","count":3,"firstVerse":1},{"id":"meunites-h4586g","name":"Meunites","kind":"person","brief":"From Canaan","count":1,"firstVerse":1},{"id":"judah-h3063g","name":"Judah","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":2,"firstVerse":3}],"places":[{"id":"ammon-h5983","name":"Ammon","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":1},{"id":"moab-h4124g","name":"Moab","kind":"place","brief":"In Edom","count":1,"firstVerse":1},{"id":"edom-h0123g","name":"Edom","kind":"place","brief":"In Edom","count":1,"firstVerse":2},{"id":"engedi-h5872","name":"Engedi","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":2}],"words":[{"base":"H3092","lemma":"יְהוֹשָׁפָט","tr":"ye·ho·sha·phat","gloss":"Jehoshaphat","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":84},{"base":"H2688","lemma":"חַצֲצֹן תָּמָר","tr":"chats·tson ta·mar","gloss":"Hazazon-tamar","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":4},{"base":"H5872","lemma":"עֵין גֶּ֫דִי","tr":"en ge·di","gloss":"Engedi","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":12},{"base":"H3063","lemma":"יְהוּדָה","tr":"ye·hu·dah","gloss":"Judah","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":820},{"base":"H1245","lemma":"בָּקַשׁ","tr":"ba·qash","gloss":"to seek","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":225},{"base":"H5984","lemma":"עַמּוֹנִי","tr":"am·mo·ni","gloss":"Meunite","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":21},{"base":"H6685","lemma":"צוֹם","tr":"tsom","gloss":"fast","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":26},{"base":"H1995","lemma":"הָמוֹן","tr":"ha·mon","gloss":"crowd","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":83},{"base":"H5676","lemma":"עֵ֫בֶר","tr":"e·ver","gloss":"side: beside","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":90},{"base":"H5983","lemma":"עַמּוֹן","tr":"am·mon","gloss":"Ammon","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":106}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"PSA","chapter":50,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"Call upon Me in the day of trouble; I will deliver you, and you will honor Me.”","from":4},{"book":"2CH","chapter":19,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"However, some good is found in you, for you have removed the Asherah poles from the land and have set your heart on seeking God.”","from":3},{"book":"DAN","chapter":9,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"So I turned my attention to the Lord God to seek Him by prayer and petition, with fasting, sackcloth, and ashes.","from":3},{"book":"GEN","chapter":14,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Then they turned back to invade En-mishpat (that is, Kadesh), and they conquered the whole territory of the Amalekites, as well as the Amorites who lived in Hazazon-tamar.","from":2},{"book":"1SA","chapter":7,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"When they had gathered at Mizpah, they drew water and poured it out before the LORD. On that day they fasted, and there they confessed, “We have sinned against the LORD.” And Samuel judged the Israelites at Mizpah.","from":3},{"book":"JER","chapter":36,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Now in the ninth month of the fifth year of Jehoiakim son of Josiah king of Judah, a fast before the LORD was proclaimed to all the people of Jerusalem and all who had come there from the cities of Judah.","from":3},{"book":"JOL","chapter":1,"verse":14,"verseEnd":14,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Consecrate a fast; proclaim a solemn assembly! Gather the elders and all the residents of the land to the house of the LORD your God, and cry out to the LORD.","from":3},{"book":"JOL","chapter":2,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"“Yet even now,” declares the LORD, “return to Me with all your heart, with fasting, weeping, and mourning.”","from":3}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"5-12":{"people":[{"id":"jehoshaphat-h3092i","name":"Jehoshaphat","kind":"person","brief":"King of Judah","count":1,"firstVerse":5},{"id":"judah-h3063g","name":"Judah","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":5},{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":2,"firstVerse":7},{"id":"abraham-h0085","name":"Abraham","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Terah","count":1,"firstVerse":7}],"places":[{"id":"jerusalem-h3389","name":"Jerusalem","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":5},{"id":"ammon-h5983","name":"Ammon","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":10},{"id":"egypt-h4714g","name":"Egypt","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":10},{"id":"moab-h4124g","name":"Moab","kind":"place","brief":"In Edom","count":1,"firstVerse":10},{"id":"seir-mount-h8165g","name":"Seir Mount","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":10}],"words":[{"base":"H3581","lemma":"כֹּחַ","tr":"ko·ach","gloss":"reptile","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":126},{"base":"H0859","lemma":"אַתָּ֫ה","tr":"at·tah","gloss":"you(m.s.)","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":1092},{"base":"H2088","lemma":"זֶה","tr":"zeh","gloss":"this","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":1176},{"base":"H3423","lemma":"יָרַשׁ","tr":"ya·rash","gloss":"to possess: possess","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":231},{"base":"H8196","lemma":"שְׁפוֹט","tr":"she·phot","gloss":"judgment","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"H9034","lemma":"הָ","tr":"ha","gloss":"her","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":490},{"base":"H5975","lemma":"עָמַד","tr":"a·mad","gloss":"to stand: stand","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":521},{"base":"H0369","lemma":"אַ֫יִן","tr":"a·yin","gloss":"nothing","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":788},{"base":"H2009","lemma":"הִנֵּה","tr":"hin·neh","gloss":"behold","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":843},{"base":"H8034","lemma":"שֵׁם","tr":"shem","gloss":"name","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":864}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"PSA","chapter":121,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":28,"source":"openbible","text":"I lift up my eyes to the hills. From where does my help come?","from":12},{"book":"PSA","chapter":121,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":28,"source":"openbible","text":"My help comes from the LORD, the Maker of heaven and earth.","from":12},{"book":"PSA","chapter":25,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":23,"source":"both","text":"My eyes are always on the LORD, for He will free my feet from the mesh.","from":12},{"book":"PSA","chapter":141,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":21,"source":"both","text":"But my eyes are fixed on You, O GOD the Lord. In You I seek refuge; do not leave my soul defenseless.","from":12},{"book":"PSA","chapter":123,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":16,"source":"openbible","text":"I lift up my eyes to You, the One enthroned in heaven.","from":12},{"book":"PSA","chapter":123,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":16,"source":"openbible","text":"As the eyes of servants look to the hand of their master, as the eyes of a maidservant look to the hand of her mistress, so our eyes are on the LORD our God until He shows us mercy.","from":12},{"book":"DEU","chapter":32,"verse":36,"verseEnd":36,"votes":15,"source":"both","text":"For the LORD will vindicate His people and have compassion on His servants when He sees that their strength is gone and no one remains, slave or free.","from":12},{"book":"2CH","chapter":6,"verse":28,"verseEnd":28,"votes":14,"source":"openbible","text":"When famine or plague comes upon the land, or blight or mildew or locusts or grasshoppers, or when their enemies besiege them in their cities, whatever plague or sickness may come,","from":9}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":3}]},"13-19":{"people":[{"id":"judah-h3063g","name":"Judah","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":4,"firstVerse":13},{"id":"levi-h3878","name":"Levi","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":2,"firstVerse":14},{"id":"asaph-h0623g","name":"Asaph","kind":"person","brief":"Returned musician","count":1,"firstVerse":14},{"id":"benaiah-h1141l","name":"Benaiah","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Jeiel","count":1,"firstVerse":14},{"id":"jahaziel-h3166j","name":"Jahaziel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Zechariah","count":1,"firstVerse":14},{"id":"jeiel-h3273j","name":"Jeiel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Mattaniah","count":1,"firstVerse":14},{"id":"mattaniah-h4983i","name":"Mattaniah","kind":"person","brief":"Father of Jeiel","count":1,"firstVerse":14},{"id":"zechariah-h2148i","name":"Zechariah","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Benaiah","count":1,"firstVerse":14},{"id":"jehoshaphat-h3092i","name":"Jehoshaphat","kind":"person","brief":"King of Judah","count":2,"firstVerse":15},{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":1,"firstVerse":19},{"id":"kohath-h6955","name":"Kohath","kind":"person","brief":"Levi's son","count":1,"firstVerse":19},{"id":"korah-h7141i","name":"Korah","kind":"person","brief":"Aaron's adversary","count":1,"firstVerse":19}],"places":[{"id":"jerusalem-h3389","name":"Jerusalem","kind":"place","brief":"","count":3,"firstVerse":15},{"id":"jeruel-h3385","name":"Jeruel","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":16},{"id":"ziz-h6732","name":"Ziz","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":16}],"words":[{"base":"H0408","lemma":"אַל","tr":"al","gloss":"not","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":724},{"base":"H3063","lemma":"יְהוּדָה","tr":"ye·hu·dah","gloss":"Judah","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":820},{"base":"H2865","lemma":"חָתַת","tr":"cha·tat","gloss":"to to be dismayed","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":52},{"base":"H4279","lemma":"מָחָר","tr":"ma·char","gloss":"tomorrow","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":52},{"base":"H9036","lemma":"כֶם","tr":"khem","gloss":"you","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":591},{"base":"H3389","lemma":"יְרוּשָׁלִַ֫ם, יְרוּשְׁלֵם","tr":"ye·ru·sha·laim","gloss":"Jerusalem","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":643},{"base":"H3092","lemma":"יְהוֹשָׁפָט","tr":"ye·ho·sha·phat","gloss":"Jehoshaphat","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":84},{"base":"H4480","lemma":"מִן־","tr":"min","gloss":"from","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":1187},{"base":"H3881","lemma":"לֵוִי","tr":"le·viy·yi","gloss":"Levi","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":291},{"base":"H3372","lemma":"יָרֵא","tr":"ya·re","gloss":"to fear","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":315}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"EXO","chapter":14,"verse":13,"verseEnd":13,"votes":41,"source":"openbible","text":"But Moses told the people, “Do not be afraid. Stand firm and you will see the LORDʼs salvation, which He will accomplish for you today; for the Egyptians you see today, you will never see again.","from":17},{"book":"EXO","chapter":14,"verse":14,"verseEnd":14,"votes":41,"source":"openbible","text":"The LORD will fight for you; you need only to be still.”","from":17},{"book":"2CH","chapter":32,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":40,"source":"openbible","text":"“Be strong and courageous! Do not be afraid or discouraged before the king of Assyria and the vast army with him, for there is a greater One with us than with him.","from":15},{"book":"2CH","chapter":32,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":40,"source":"both","text":"With him is only the arm of flesh, but with us is the LORD our God to help us and to fight our battles.” So the people were strengthened by the words of Hezekiah king of Judah.","from":15},{"book":"DEU","chapter":31,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":37,"source":"both","text":"Be strong and courageous; do not be afraid or terrified of them, for it is the LORD your God who goes with you; He will never leave you nor forsake you.”","from":15},{"book":"EXO","chapter":14,"verse":13,"verseEnd":13,"votes":34,"source":"openbible","text":"But Moses told the people, “Do not be afraid. Stand firm and you will see the LORDʼs salvation, which He will accomplish for you today; for the Egyptians you see today, you will never see again.","from":15},{"book":"EXO","chapter":14,"verse":14,"verseEnd":14,"votes":34,"source":"openbible","text":"The LORD will fight for you; you need only to be still.”","from":15},{"book":"DEU","chapter":31,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":33,"source":"both","text":"The LORD Himself goes before you; He will be with you. He will never leave you nor forsake you. Do not be afraid or discouraged.”","from":15}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":3},{"id":"exodus-family","title":"Moses and his circle","people":2}]},"20-25":{"people":[{"id":"judah-h3063g","name":"Judah","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":3,"firstVerse":20},{"id":"jehoshaphat-h3092i","name":"Jehoshaphat","kind":"person","brief":"King of Judah","count":2,"firstVerse":20}],"places":[{"id":"jerusalem-h3389","name":"Jerusalem","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":20},{"id":"tekoa-h8620","name":"Tekoa","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":20},{"id":"ammon-h5983","name":"Ammon","kind":"place","brief":"","count":2,"firstVerse":22},{"id":"moab-h4124g","name":"Moab","kind":"place","brief":"In Edom","count":2,"firstVerse":22},{"id":"seir-mount-h8165g","name":"Seir Mount","kind":"place","brief":"","count":2,"firstVerse":22},{"id":"seir-h8165a","name":"Seir","kind":"place","brief":"In Edom","count":1,"firstVerse":23}],"words":[{"base":"H8165","lemma":"שֵׂעִיר","tr":"se·ir","gloss":"Seir","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":39},{"base":"H0539","lemma":"אָמַן","tr":"a·man","gloss":"be faithful","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":105},{"base":"H6297","lemma":"פֶּ֫גֶר","tr":"pe·ger","gloss":"corpse","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":22},{"base":"H0962","lemma":"בָּזַז","tr":"ba·zaz","gloss":"to plunder","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":43},{"base":"H5975","lemma":"עָמַד","tr":"a·mad","gloss":"to stand: stand","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":521},{"base":"H7998","lemma":"שָׁלָל","tr":"sha·lal","gloss":"spoil","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":73},{"base":"H3092","lemma":"יְהוֹשָׁפָט","tr":"ye·ho·sha·phat","gloss":"Jehoshaphat","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":84},{"base":"H3063","lemma":"יְהוּדָה","tr":"ye·hu·dah","gloss":"Judah","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":820},{"base":"H5983","lemma":"עַמּוֹן","tr":"am·mon","gloss":"Ammon","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":106},{"base":"H3318","lemma":"יָצָא","tr":"ya·tsa","gloss":"to come out: come","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":1067}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"JHN","chapter":14,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":31,"source":"both","text":"“Do not let your hearts be troubled. You believe in God; believe in Me as well.","from":20},{"book":"JHN","chapter":11,"verse":40,"verseEnd":40,"votes":29,"source":"both","text":"Jesus replied, “Did I not tell you that if you believed, you would see the glory of God?”","from":20},{"book":"HEB","chapter":11,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":29,"source":"both","text":"And without faith it is impossible to please God. For anyone who approaches Him must believe that He exists and that He rewards those who earnestly seek Him.","from":20},{"book":"ROM","chapter":8,"verse":31,"verseEnd":31,"votes":28,"source":"both","text":"What then shall we say in response to these things? If God is for us, who can be against us?","from":20},{"book":"LUK","chapter":16,"verse":31,"verseEnd":31,"votes":27,"source":"both","text":"Then Abraham said to him, ‘If they do not listen to Moses and the Prophets, they will not be persuaded even if someone rises from the dead.’”","from":20},{"book":"ISA","chapter":26,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":25,"source":"both","text":"You will keep in perfect peace the steadfast of mind, because he trusts in You.","from":20},{"book":"JHN","chapter":13,"verse":20,"verseEnd":20,"votes":25,"source":"both","text":"Truly, truly, I tell you, whoever receives the one I send receives Me, and whoever receives Me receives the One who sent Me.”","from":20},{"book":"JHN","chapter":5,"verse":46,"verseEnd":46,"votes":21,"source":"openbible","text":"If you had believed Moses, you would believe Me, because he wrote about Me.","from":20}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"26-30":{"people":[{"id":"jehoshaphat-h3092i","name":"Jehoshaphat","kind":"person","brief":"King of Judah","count":2,"firstVerse":27},{"id":"judah-h3063g","name":"Judah","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":27},{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":1,"firstVerse":29}],"places":[{"id":"beracah-valley-h1294h","name":"Beracah Valley","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":26},{"id":"jerusalem-h3389","name":"Jerusalem","kind":"place","brief":"","count":2,"firstVerse":27}],"words":[{"base":"H1294","lemma":"בְּרָכָה","tr":"be·ra·khah","gloss":"Beracah","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":3},{"base":"H3389","lemma":"יְרוּשָׁלִַ֫ם, יְרוּשְׁלֵם","tr":"ye·ru·sha·laim","gloss":"Jerusalem","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":643},{"base":"H6010","lemma":"עֵ֫מֶק","tr":"e·meq","gloss":"Valley (of Achor)","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":69},{"base":"H3092","lemma":"יְהוֹשָׁפָט","tr":"ye·ho·sha·phat","gloss":"Jehoshaphat","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":84},{"base":"H0341","lemma":"אֹיֵב","tr":"o·yev","gloss":"enemy","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":282},{"base":"H7725","lemma":"שׁוּב","tr":"shuv","gloss":"to return: return","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":1057},{"base":"H2689","lemma":"חֲצֹצְרָה","tr":"cha·tso·tse·rah","gloss":"trumpet","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":29},{"base":"H5035","lemma":"נֵ֫בֶל","tr":"ne·vel","gloss":"bag","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":38},{"base":"H6950","lemma":"קָהַל","tr":"qa·hal","gloss":"to gather","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":39},{"base":"H8252","lemma":"שָׁקַט","tr":"sha·qat","gloss":"to quiet","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":41}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"2CH","chapter":15,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"And all Judah rejoiced over the oath, for they had sworn it with all their heart. They had sought Him earnestly, and He was found by them. So the LORD gave them rest on every side.","from":30},{"book":"2CH","chapter":17,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"And the dread of the LORD fell upon all the kingdoms of the lands that surrounded Judah, so that they did not make war against Jehoshaphat.","from":29},{"book":"2CH","chapter":14,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"Because the land was at peace, Asa built fortified cities in Judah. In those days no one made war with him, because the LORD had given him rest.","from":30},{"book":"2CH","chapter":14,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"So he said to the people of Judah, “Let us build these cities and surround them with walls and towers, with doors and bars. The land is still ours because we have sought the LORD our God. We have sought Him and He has given us rest on every side.” So they built and prospered.","from":30},{"book":"GEN","chapter":28,"verse":19,"verseEnd":19,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"and he called that place Bethel, though previously the city had been named Luz.","from":26},{"book":"GEN","chapter":32,"verse":20,"verseEnd":20,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"You are also to say, ‘Look, your servant Jacob is right behind us.’” For he thought, “I will appease Esau with the gift that is going before me. After that I can face him, and perhaps he will accept me.”","from":26},{"book":"GEN","chapter":35,"verse":5,"verseEnd":5,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"As they set out, a terror from God fell over the surrounding cities, so that they did not pursue Jacobʼs sons.","from":29},{"book":"EXO","chapter":15,"verse":1,"verseEnd":19,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Then Moses and the Israelites sang this song to the LORD: “I will sing to the LORD, for He is highly exalted. The horse and rider He has thrown into the sea. The LORD is my strength and my song, and He has become my salvation. He is my God, and I will praise Him, my fatherʼs God, and I will exalt Him. The LORD is a warrior, the LORD is His name. Pharaohʼs chariots and army He has cast into the sea; the finest of his officers are drowned in the Red Sea. The depths have covered them; they sank there like a stone.","from":26}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":2}]},"31-37":{"people":[{"id":"jehoshaphat-h3092i","name":"Jehoshaphat","kind":"person","brief":"King of Judah","count":4,"firstVerse":31},{"id":"judah-h3063g","name":"Judah","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":2,"firstVerse":31},{"id":"azubah-h5806g","name":"Azubah","kind":"person","brief":"Daughter of Shilhi","count":1,"firstVerse":31},{"id":"shilhi-h7977","name":"Shilhi","kind":"person","brief":"Father of Azubah","count":1,"firstVerse":31},{"id":"asa-h0609g","name":"Asa","kind":"person","brief":"King of Judah","count":1,"firstVerse":32},{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":2,"firstVerse":34},{"id":"hanani-h2607g","name":"Hanani","kind":"person","brief":"A prophet","count":1,"firstVerse":34},{"id":"jehu-h3058g","name":"Jehu","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Hanani","count":1,"firstVerse":34},{"id":"ahaziah-h0274g","name":"Ahaziah","kind":"person","brief":"King of N. Israel","count":2,"firstVerse":35},{"id":"dodavahu-h1735","name":"Dodavahu","kind":"person","brief":"Father of Eliezer","count":1,"firstVerse":37},{"id":"eliezer-h0461l","name":"Eliezer","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Dodavahu","count":1,"firstVerse":37}],"places":[{"id":"jerusalem-h3389","name":"Jerusalem","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":31},{"id":"tarshish-h8659h","name":"Tarshish","kind":"place","brief":"In Benjamin","count":2,"firstVerse":36},{"id":"ezion-geber-h6100","name":"Ezion-geber","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":36},{"id":"mareshah-h4762g","name":"Mareshah","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":37}],"words":[{"base":"H3092","lemma":"יְהוֹשָׁפָט","tr":"ye·ho·sha·phat","gloss":"Jehoshaphat","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":84},{"base":"H2266","lemma":"חָבַר","tr":"cha·var","gloss":"to unite","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":29},{"base":"H0591","lemma":"אֳנִיָּה","tr":"o·niy·yah","gloss":"fleet","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":31},{"base":"H6100","lemma":"עֶצְיוֹן גֶּ֫בֶר","tr":"ets·yon ge·ver","gloss":"Ezion-geber","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":14},{"base":"H4427","lemma":"מָלַךְ","tr":"ma·lakh","gloss":"to reign","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":348},{"base":"H8659","lemma":"תַּרְשִׁישׁ","tr":"tar·shish","gloss":"Tarshish","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":28},{"base":"H0274","lemma":"אֲחַזְיָ֫הוּ","tr":"a·chaz·yah","gloss":"Ahaziah","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":37},{"base":"H5973","lemma":"עִם","tr":"im","gloss":"with","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":1051},{"base":"H5493","lemma":"סוּר","tr":"sur","gloss":"to turn aside: remove","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":300},{"base":"H2568","lemma":"חָמֵשׁ","tr":"cha·mesh","gloss":"five","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":343}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"1KI","chapter":22,"verse":48,"verseEnd":48,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"Jehoshaphat built ships of Tarshish to go to Ophir for gold, but they never set sail, because they were wrecked at Ezion-geber.","from":35},{"book":"1KI","chapter":22,"verse":49,"verseEnd":49,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"At that time Ahaziah son of Ahab said to Jehoshaphat, “Let my servants sail with your servants,” but Jehoshaphat refused.","from":35},{"book":"2CH","chapter":17,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"And his heart took delight in the ways of the LORD; furthermore, he removed the high places and Asherah poles from Judah.","from":33},{"book":"PRO","chapter":13,"verse":20,"verseEnd":20,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"He who walks with the wise will become wise, but the companion of fools will be destroyed.","from":37},{"book":"DEU","chapter":29,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Yet to this day the LORD has not given you a mind to understand, eyes to see, or ears to hear.","from":33},{"book":"JOS","chapter":7,"verse":11,"verseEnd":12,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Israel has sinned; they have transgressed My covenant that I commanded them, and they have taken some of what was devoted to destruction. Indeed, they have stolen and lied, and they have put these things with their own possessions. This is why the Israelites cannot stand against their enemies. They will turn their backs and run from their enemies, because they themselves have been set apart for destruction. I will no longer be with you unless you remove from among you whatever is devoted to destruction.","from":37},{"book":"1SA","chapter":7,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Then Samuel said to all the house of Israel, “If you are returning to the LORD with all your hearts, then put away the foreign gods and Ashtoreths among you, prepare your hearts for the LORD, and serve Him only. And He will deliver you from the hand of the Philistines.”","from":33},{"book":"1KI","chapter":9,"verse":26,"verseEnd":26,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"King Solomon also assembled a fleet of ships at Ezion-geber, which is near Eloth in Edom, on the shore of the Red Sea.","from":36}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":2}]}}